      "content": "thanks, that helps a lot. i'm just so paranoid because it feels like every time i document something, the next \"mistake\" happens faster. like it's a cycle. i'm worried if i confront them now, they'll just double down on making me look incompetent or crazy to cover their tracks. if they're actually trying to gaslight me into leaving without benefits, what are the subtle 'red flags' i should look for to prove they're testing my mental stability instead of just being bad at management?",
